{
  "code": "def summarize_vdb_vulns(\n    vulnerability_vdb_store: pd.DataFrame,\n    vulnerability_cisa_kev: pd.DataFrame,\n    vulnerability_epss_scores: pd.DataFrame,\n    vulnerability_cwe_categories: pd.DataFrame,\n) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    # legacy: Phase G  (phase_g_vdb_summary CFA:3771)\n    \"\"\"Roll up per-CVE vdb records into the per-package report-only rollup (7 d TTL).\n\n    ``vulnerability_vdb_store`` is now the ``VDBStoreDataset`` (B5 landed the FLIP): its\n    ``load()`` parses the vdb store + applies ``coerce_cvss_score`` at the read boundary\n    (Gap G-3 / DW-B2-2), so this node receives an already-parsed + coerced per-CVE frame\n    (``package_name``, ``cve_id``, ``cvss_score``, optional ``cwe_id``, ``severity``). It\n    applies the KEV overlay (``apply_kev_overlay``,\n    AC-3(a)) + the v8.6.0 EPSS/CWE aggregation (``aggregate_v8_6_0_overlays``,\n    max-EPSS/None-not-0), then rolls up per package.\n\n    **REPORT-ONLY** (AC-2): this rollup is ``packages.vuln_*``, kept for backward-compat,\n    synced COALESCE-to-existing (``_phase_g_sync_current_rollup`` CFA:6990/7029-7030). It\n    is NOT query-time-correct — ``v_current_version_vulns`` (backed by ``per_version_vulns``)\n    is. Output ``vulnerability_package_rollup``: ``package_name``, ``vuln_count``,\n    ``vuln_critical_high``, ``vuln_kev_affecting_current``, ``vuln_max_cvss``,\n    ``vuln_max_epss_score``.\"\"\"\n    cols = [\n        \"package_name\",\n        \"vuln_count\",\n        \"vuln_critical_high\",\n        \"vuln_kev_affecting_current\",\n        \"vuln_max_cvss\",\n        \"vuln_max_epss_score\",\n    ]\n    vdb = vulnerability_vdb_store\n    if vdb is None or vdb.empty or not {\"package_name\", \"cve_id\"} <= set(vdb.columns):\n        return pd.DataFrame(columns=cols)\n    work = vdb.copy()\n    if \"cvss_score\" not in work.columns:\n        work[\"cvss_score\"] = pd.NA\n    work[\"is_kev\"] = apply_kev_overlay(work, vulnerability_cisa_kev).values\n    work = aggregate_v8_6_0_overlays(work, vulnerability_epss_scores, vulnerability_cwe_categories)\n\n    # A CVE with no package_name cannot be attributed to a rollup row — drop it\n    # EXPLICITLY (a groupby drops NaN keys SILENTLY; making it visible is the review\n    # fix). NOTE: `vuln_kev_affecting_current` here is a PACKAGE-WIDE KEV count over all\n    # vdb rows for the package — the rollup is REPORT-ONLY (AC-2); the version-accurate\n    # KEV-affecting-current lives in per_version_vulns -> v_current_version_vulns.\n    work = work.dropna(subset=[\"package_name\"])\n    records = []\n    for pkg, grp in work.groupby(\"package_name\"):\n        cvss = pd.to_numeric(grp[\"cvss_score\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n        epss = pd.to_numeric(grp.get(\"epss_score\", pd.Series(dtype=float)), errors=\"coerce\")\n        crit_high = int((cvss >= 7.0).sum())\n        records.append(\n            {\n                \"package_name\": pkg,\n                \"vuln_count\": int(len(grp)),\n                \"vuln_critical_high\": crit_high,\n                \"vuln_kev_affecting_current\": int(grp[\"is_kev\"].sum()),\n                # None-not-0.0: max over an all-empty set is NaN (unknown), not 0.\n                \"vuln_max_cvss\": None if cvss.dropna().empty else float(cvss.max()),\n                \"vuln_max_epss_score\": None if epss.dropna().empty else float(epss.max()),\n            }\n        )\n    return pd.DataFrame(records, columns=cols).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
